{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And you said, etc.</b> Rabbi Jonah the grammarian said that נָנוּס is from the decree of נס, like the meaning of נִרְכַּב that has something after it, and some say it is as it sounds: you flee, and your pursuers put you to flight:" "<b>Upon the swift.</b> An adjective for the horse, or [read: like] light for the camel."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {0 "Resolved Rabbi Jonah the grammarian as the standard identification of רבי יונה המדקדק; the phrase 'that has something after it' refers to a verb followed by another verb in sequence.", 1 "The bracketed [צ\"ל כמו] is a scribal correction notation in the source text indicating the word או should read כמו; I have rendered it as '[read: like]' to flag this editorial intervention."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:01.506343330Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}